IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-vintages`
IMPORT `g7-commencement`
IMPORT `g7-art21-23-expressions`
IMPORT `g7-art24-25-powers`
IMPORT `g7-art37-43-final`
IMPORT `g7-tests-fixtures-expressions`

-- g7-tests-red: tests that are MEANT to fail, and are counted (15).  Each one asserts the answer of the OTHER reading of a fork against the reading taken, or a claim the survey or the brief made that the
-- instruments in inputs/amending/ correct.  Every one of them fails; that is the finding it records (the two readings give different answers at the discriminating case), and the file doubles as proof that this
-- harness can fail.  check.sh lists this module in expected_failed with the count 15.  No other module of group G7 contains a failing assertion.

§ `Tests that are meant to fail`

`other F7.1` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.1`
`other F7.11` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.11`

GIVEN jersey IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entity
`an entity for the red tests` jersey MEANS
    Entity WITH name IS "An entity"
              , `standing on the register` IS `not on the register`
              , `kinds of entity` IS (IF jersey THEN LIST `a company` ELSE LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`)
              , `is a Jersey entity` IS jersey
              , governors IS EMPTY
              , purposes IS EMPTY

GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`no Order fixes a date` MEANS NOTHING

`a penalty of imprisonment alone for 24 months` MEANS `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS JUST 24, fine IS `no fine is provided`

§§ `The other reading of each fork, asserted against the reading taken (14 findings, one per fork)`

-- F7.1: the other reading puts the whole of 27 February 2024 in the new text, so the day alone is answered; the reading taken refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` (YMD 2024 2 27) `other F7.1`
-- F7.2: seven clear days (the eighth day): 9 October 2025 + 8 = 17 October; the reading taken, and the Table, give 16 October.
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the day an instrument made on a day comes into force 7 days after` (YMD 2025 10 9) `fav` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 17
-- F7.3: the Table read in present numbers puts the present Article 41 in the remainder (not in force on 1 January 2018); the reading taken puts it in stage 1.
#ASSERT NOT `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`an Article of the Law as now numbered` 41) (YMD 2018 1 1) `fav`
-- F7.4: the knowing offence displaces the strict one: only paragraph (2) is made out by scenario 05; the reading taken makes out both.
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` (`an entity for the red tests` TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE `scenario 05` `fav` EQUALS LIST `paragraph (2) of Article 21`
-- F7.5: the words “or other advantage” carried to paragraph (4): scenario 11 (to induce volunteers to give their time) contravenes 21(4); as printed it does not.
#ASSERT `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` (`an entity for the red tests` TRUE) FALSE `scenario 11` `fav`
-- F7.6: an unincorporated association is within Article 37(1): a governor who connived is also guilty; as written he is not.
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`Facts for Article 37` WITH `kind of body` IS `an unincorporated association`, `the body committed an offence under this Law` IS TRUE, `consent or connivance is proved` IS TRUE, capacity IS `a governor of the body corporate`, `how the person comes within the capacity` IS `holds the capacity`) `fav`
-- F7.7: the date of service is the date the notice is sent (2026-06-01); the reading taken, the date of receipt, gives 2026-06-03.
#ASSERT `Art 38 the date on which the notice is served` (YMD 2026 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 3)) `no Order fixes a date` `fav` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
-- F7.8: a term of 2 years is 730 days: a sentence of 731 days from 2027-03-01 is beyond it; the reading taken (24 calendar months, 731 days from that day) puts it within.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2027 3 1) `fav`
-- F7.9: a Part is in force when any of its Articles is: Part 8 (Article 32 in force since 2014) is in force on 2015-06-01; the reading taken waits for all of them.
#ASSERT `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`a Part of the Law` 8) (YMD 2015 6 1) `fav`
-- F7.10: any listed capacity for any body: a director of a limited liability partnership is also guilty; as printed only a partner is.
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`Facts for Article 37` WITH `kind of body` IS `a limited liability partnership`, `the body committed an offence under this Law` IS TRUE, `consent or connivance is proved` IS TRUE, capacity IS `a director of the body corporate`, `how the person comes within the capacity` IS `holds the capacity`) `fav`
-- F7.11: the day after the named day is the first day in force: Part 1 is not in force on 21 November 2014 itself; the reading taken says it is.
#ASSERT NOT `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`a Part of the Law` 1) (YMD 2014 11 21) `fav`
-- F7.12: Article 22 defines the term for Article 21 only: for Article 2(10)(b) the question is refused; the reading taken answers it.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity for the purpose of Article 2(10)(b)` (`Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH `established under` IS `the law of the United Kingdom or of a jurisdiction that is part of the United Kingdom`, `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS TRUE, `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS TRUE, `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS FALSE) FALSE `fav`
-- F7.13: an offence adapted from Articles 21 to 23 may keep its imprisonment; the reading taken caps every offence of the Regulations at a fine.
#ASSERT `Art 24 the Regulations may attach this penalty to the offence` `a penalty of imprisonment alone for 24 months` TRUE `fav`
-- F7.14: an Order under Article 2(2) can make consequential amendments; the reading taken says only Regulations can.
#ASSERT `Art 39 an Order under Article 2(2) may make a consequential amendment of another provision of the Law` `fav`

§§ `A claim the instruments correct (1 finding)`

-- The brief described the remainder of the staged commencement as including the original Article 44(2) and (3).  R&O.17/2018 Article 2 gives the remainder as what Article 44(2) of the Law or Article 1 of the Act did
-- not bring into force, so the original Article 44 (all of it) is in stage 1, and the remainder is Part 6 and the original Article 41.
#ASSERT `Commencement: the stage in which the unit was brought into force` (`an Article of the Law as originally numbered` 44) `fav` EQUALS `stage 3: 1 January 2019`
